Implement QImode multiplication without widening the operands to a libcall.
Signed and unsigned products agree modulo 256. Use a full-D unsigned MUL,
then copy its low byte. Signed HI widening products still use mulhi3.

Add the same-operand alternative to umulqihi3: reload/postreload may put
both input bytes in B, so copy B to A before MUL. The other alternative
loads the second operand from memory/immediate. Require the first input
in B, the byte register MUL actually reads, rather than the broader q class.

Without mulqi3, optabs.c widens narrow products to mulhi3 with paradoxical
HI subregs of QI pseudos. Those are valid with unspecified high bits, but the
m6809 reload constraints cannot allocate them in A_REGS across a call.

--- a/gcc/config/m6809/m6809.md
+++ b/gcc/config/m6809/m6809.md
@@ -958,12 +958,30 @@
 (define_insn "umulqihi3"
-   [(set (match_operand:HI 0 "register_operand" "=d")
-    (mult:HI (zero_extend:HI (match_operand:QI 1 "general_operand" "%q"))
-    (match_operand:QI 2 "general_operand" "tmK")))]
+   [(set (match_operand:HI 0 "register_operand" "=d,d")
+    (mult:HI (zero_extend:HI (match_operand:QI 1 "general_operand" "%B,B"))
+    (match_operand:QI 2 "general_operand" "1,tmK")))]
   ""
-  "lda\t%2\t;umulqihi3\;mul"
-  [(set_attr "length" "3")])
+  "@
+   tfr\tb,a\t;umulqihi3: same byte\;mul
+   lda\t%2\t;umulqihi3\;mul"
+  [(set_attr "length" "3,3")])
+
+
+; MUL is unsigned, but its low byte also implements signed multiplication
+; modulo 256. Keep the HI output so reload sees the whole D clobber.
+(define_expand "mulqi3"
+  [(set (match_operand:QI 0 "nonimmediate_operand" "")
+    (mult:QI (match_operand:QI 1 "general_operand" "")
+    (match_operand:QI 2 "general_operand" "")))]
+  ""
+{
+  rtx product = gen_reg_rtx (HImode);
+
+  emit_insn (gen_umulqihi3 (product, operands[1], operands[2]));
+  emit_move_insn (operands[0], gen_lowpart (QImode, product));
+  DONE;
+})
-
-
+
+
 ; Expand a 16x16 multiplication into either a libcall or a shift.
 ; If the second operand is a small constant, use the above form.
 ; Otherwise, do a libcall.
